    "description": "Source: Open Questions doc, Q8 comment thread. Emily Vandenberg asked TWO questions:\n\n1\\. 'can we have both options for auto complete + manual button' — ANSWERED (no auto-completion, manual Complete button only).\n\n2\\. 'what happens to the record upon completion? does it become locked or is it still editable.' — NEVER ANSWERED.\n\n⚠️ The thread is marked RESOLVED in Google Docs, so this will look closed in Emily's queue and will not resurface on its own. Needs an explicit re-ask.\n\nWhy it matters: it determines whether the Complete action locks the record (like the fraud flag does), and whether Ops needs an unlock path. Affects BUILD-34 (record lock automations) and the Complete screen flow.\n\nJumpr recommendation to put forward: lock rep edit on Completion, keep Ops editable, mirroring the fraud-lock pattern already built — reps get a consistent 'record is final' signal and Ops retain a correction path.\n\nAlso still open from the same doc:\n\n* Q5 — rep-facing field list for the Deal object. Emily promised it 'by EOW' on 2026-07-24; never landed, and the comment is marked resolved. Hard blocker on BUILD-64. Re-ask.\n\n* Q6 — fraud flag impact on Player status. Jumpr's Phase-1-manual proposal has had no response. See DECISION-02 / DECISION-03.\n\n",
